<title>UK: Sullom Voe liftings up, over 40 pct to U.S.</title>
<headline>Sullom Voe liftings up, over 40 pct to U.S.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Loadings of Brent Blend crude oil from the Sullom Voe terminal in the Shetland Islands rose by 83,372 tonnes to 771,292 tonnes in the week ending August 27, according to data published by the Shetland Islands Council.</p>
<p>Over 40 percent of the Brent sailed to destinations in the United States. The balance was evenly divided between British and northwest European refineries.  </p>
<p>Below is a list of loadings:</p>
<p> DATE    VESSEL		   DESTINATION	 CARGO (TONNES)</p>
<p> 22/8    Independence	   U.S. Gulf	   258,618</p>
<p>	   Fosna		    Kalundborg	   75,732</p>
<p> 23/8    Manhattan		Tranmere	     69,277</p>
<p> 24/8    Mastera		  Porvoo		131,735</p>
<p> 26/8    Alandia Pearl	  Milford Haven	69,193</p>
<p> 27/8    Solena		   Fawley		 82,264</p>
<p>	   Hitra		    Portland Maine     84,473</p>
<p> WK ENDING U.K.     NWE	AMERICAS  MED     OTHER    TOTAL</p>
<p>  27/8     220,734  207,467  343,091   --	--	 771,292</p>
<p>  20/8     152,767  361,693  173,460   --	--	 687,920</p>
<p>  13/8     217,337  208,345  128,132   --	--	 553,814</p>
<p>  6/8	138,518  281,066  133,961	     69,236   622,781</p>
